-- title:
--   If $0\le a\le b$, then $a$ lies in the hereditary subalgebra generated by $b$
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a possibly non-unital C$^*$-algebra, ordered by its positive cone. For $h\in A$ write
--   $$\operatorname{Her}(h)=\overline{\{\,h\,x\,h^{*}\ :\ x\in A\,\}}$$
--   for the norm closure of the set of sandwiches $hxh^*$. It is a closed $*$-subalgebra of $A$, and for positive $h$ it is the hereditary C$^*$-subalgebra generated by $h$.
--
--   **Theorem.** For all $a,b\in A$,
--   $$0\le a\le b\ \Longrightarrow\ a\in\operatorname{Her}(b).$$
--
--   This is the hereditary property of the closure of $bAb^*$, expressed through the order. It makes $\operatorname{Her}$ monotone on positive elements: $0\le a\le b$ implies $\operatorname{Her}(a)\subseteq\operatorname{Her}(b)$. Consequently, two positive elements that dominate each other up to positive constants generate the same hereditary subalgebra. This is used repeatedly when hereditary subalgebras are compared and transported.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `Her b` is the topological closure of the range of $x\mapsto b\,x\,b^*$. The order on $A$ is any partial order making $A$ a star-ordered ring, which is necessarily the positive-cone order.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/CStarAlgebra/PureInfiniteness/Hereditary.lean#L457-L476

